# Neo Learn FM parameters (docs/specs/neo-learn.md, neo-learn-controls.md A1 and A2.3). The order is permanent: songs and
# presets store values by position. The 12 controls are the six core ones, then the six global ones (Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release,
# Unison / Spread, Output). Each has a snake_case id, and the Explain text (How, Sound; the description is the How line).
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLearnFM
namespace NeoBuzz.LearnFm
class NeoLearnFMMachine
tracks 16
summary Teaching FM synth: one Dye Essence patch driven by 12 controls. A sine carrier phase-modulated by a modulator at an exact ratio (whole and half ratios have detents), with an index that follows its own decay envelope and the note velocity, modulator feedback, a high-ratio third operator, an ADSR, unison and an output gain. Every control says what it does and what you will hear. Use it for electric pianos, bells, FM basses and glassy leads, or to learn how frequency modulation works.

group Core
ModRatio         "Mod Ratio" 0 1000 500 exp 0.25 16 × 2 detent=0.5
    id mod_ratio
    how Sets the frequency ratio of the primary modulator oscillator relative to the audible carrier oscillator.
    sound Whole numbers (1x, 2x, 4x) yield musical, woody, or electric piano tones; fractional ratios create clangorous bells.
FmIndex          "FM Depth" 0 1000 350 pct
    id fm_index
    how Controls the amplitude of the modulator feeding the carrier's phase input, determining sideband density.
    sound At 0% the synth is a pure sine wave; raising it adds glassy harmonics up to aggressive metallic growls.
ModDecay         "Mod Decay" 0 1000 583 time 0.005 5
    id mod_decay
    how Sets the decay time of the dedicated envelope that controls FM Depth over the course of a note.
    sound Short decay creates a bright metallic transient that quickly settles into a warm body (classic EP and FM bass).
Feedback         "Feedback" 0 1000 0 pct
    id feedback
    how Routes the modulator's output back into its own phase input.
    sound Pushes the modulator from a smooth sine wave into a gritty sawtooth or chaotic digital noise.
Op3Harmonic      "Metallic Edge" 0 1000 0 pct
    id op3_harmonic
    how Blends in a high-ratio third operator (M2) with a fast transient envelope.
    sound Adds glassy tine click for electric pianos or sharp vocal bite for modern FM basslines.
VelSensitivity   "Velocity to FM" 0 1000 500 pct
    id vel_sensitivity
    how Scales the maximum FM Depth and Metallic Edge based on how hard a MIDI note is struck.
    sound Soft notes play warm and rounded while hard notes bark with bright FM overtones.

group Global
EnvAttack        "Attack" 0 1000 250 time 0.0005 5
    id env_attack
    how Sets the time required for the note's amplitude (and routed envelope modulation) to ramp from silence to full peak after a note-on trigger.
    sound Low values create immediate, percussive plucks; high values produce slow, swelling pads.
EnvDecay         "Decay" 0 1000 594 time 0.005 8
    id env_decay
    how Controls how long it takes for the signal to drop from peak level down to the sustain level while a key remains held.
    sound Short decay makes notes snappy and tight; longer decay gives a gradual piano- or bell-like fade.
EnvSustain       "Sustain" 0 1000 700 pct
    id env_sustain
    how Defines the steady-state volume level maintained for as long as a note is held after the Attack and Decay stages complete.
    sound At 0% the synth behaves like a plucked or struck instrument; at 100% it holds full organ-like volume.
EnvRelease       "Release" 0 1000 515 time 0.005 10
    id env_release
    how Sets the time required for the sound to fade from its current level to complete silence after the note is released.
    sound Short release stops notes abruptly; long release leaves an ambient tail that blends chords together.
UnisonDetune     "Unison / Spread" 0 1000 0 pct
    id unison_detune
    how 0% plays one voice per note; above 0% each note plays 5 detuned, stereo-spread voices (3 in Additive, Granular and Spectral), with detune (up to ±50 cents) and width growing with the value.
    sound Thickens thin waveforms into wide, chorus-like stereo leads and pads.
OutputGain       "Output" 0 1000 529 db -36 12
    id output_gain
    how Sets the level after synthesis. There is no limiter (NeoBuzz mixes in floating point); a clip light shows when the output passes 0 dBFS.
    sound Controls overall loudness; keep the clip light dark when the next machine expects levels at or below 0 dBFS.

# What the machine measures (NeoLearnFMMachine.Readings, machine_readings): the output after Output, in dBFS.
reading rms_db dB | The output's RMS over about half a second (-inf: silence)
reading peak_db dB | The output's peak, falling 20 dB a second (-inf: silence)
reading active_voices notes | Notes sounding now (unison voices belong to their note)
